        "original_id": "b5260046-1e02-565b-8a6a-261d1c3e3441",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Richard Donchian\n- Organizations: System of a Down\n- Places: Glendale, California; Hartford, Connecticut\n- Works: The Metro\n- Topics: Armenian-American identity; heavy metal; commodities and futures trading; managed futures; song covers\n\nFacts:\n- Richard Donchian was born in September 1905 in Hartford, Connecticut.\n- Richard Donchian was an Armenian-American commodities and futures trader and a pioneer in managed futures.\n- System of a Down formed in 1994 in Glendale, California.\n- System of a Down is an Armenian-American heavy metal band also known as System and abbreviated as SOAD.\n- The song \"The Metro\" has been covered by several artists, including System of a Down, Alkaline Trio, John Frusciante, Hannah Fury, Idle Warship, and The Interrupters.\n- Richard Donchian died in 1993.",
